-- lib/derive.cub — generic programming over the data table (PLAN.md revision 7.9, 6 Nov 2026, git 2ca8d747aaa5:PLAN.md, §18.13 “F31–F32 — Reflection and certificates”, its part F31: deriving as terms
-- over the data table producing codes). derive-eq d: the code of a decidable equality on the data type
-- d, read off its constructors' shapes (lib/std.cub data-shape, the field kinds lib/check.cub reads off
-- the telescopes): a word field compares by %weq, a recursive field by the hypothesis the case provides,
-- a primitive by the machine's equality on it, a field of another data type by that type's derived
-- equality; constructors with dimensions (higher inductive types) and other field types are not covered
-- (none). derive-show d: the code of a function D → List Word writing a value in preorder. Every
-- definition here is checked at its signature; a derivation through other data types goes at most 64
-- types deep (der-depth). The codes evaluate (eval-g) and quote like any other.
import "core.cub"
import "prim.cub"
